==Arachne

=died1
#speaker:Athena
Arachne... yeah, you two are kinda alike. She, just like you, had no problem showing disrespect to the gods.

#speaker:Apistos
I’ve heard stories. If it were up to her, I bet she’d have woven a tapestry with Zeus and a lightning bolt right up his backside.

#speaker: Athena
Apistos,you’re walking on thin ice. That’s straight-up disrespect to the gods!

#speaker:Apistos
Thanks, I’ll take that as a compliment. To be honest, I never really respected you all much in the first place—and it turns out, I’m not the first, and definitely won’t be the last. You’ve given me plenty of reasons...

#speaker:Athena
I’m so done with your chatter! Just get going already!
->DONE

=died2
#speaker:Athena
Arachne again? Should I be worried she’s gonna sway you to her side?

#speaker:Apistos
Where could I possibly run from a goddess with such a terrible sense of humor?

#speaker:Athena
Hey, my humor’s just fine unlike your parents' ... Seems like they're missed the memo... Who in their right mind would actually name their kid like that?

#spekaer:Apistos
My name means “unbeliever.” Kind of ironic, huh?

#speaker:Athena
And at the same time, it’s the name of a little fish.

#speaker:Apistos
Man, I just want to end this conversation as fast as possible…

#speaker:Athena
Easy! Just go out there and fight! Come on little fish!
->DONE

=died3
